-- Chapter 5: How the present state was formed
Mizoram, Wikipedia: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mizoram
Arunachal Pradesh, Wikipedia: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arunachal_Pradesh
Dispur, Wikipedia: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dispur
TO VERIFY before publishing: the timeline line saying Shillong was the capital from 1874.$t$, date '2026-11-24' from public.content where slug = $t$formation-of-assam$t$ on conflict do nothing;
1874: Assam is separated from Bengal and becomes a {{term:chief-commissioner-province|Chief Commissioner's province}}, with Shillong as its capital.
1905: After the Partition of Bengal, Assam becomes part of the new province of Eastern Bengal and Assam.
1912: Assam becomes a separate province again.
1937: The Assam Legislative Assembly is formed, in Shillong.
1947: At Partition, most of Sylhet district goes to East Pakistan after a {{term:referendum}}. The Karimganj sub-division stays in Assam.
1950: Assam becomes a state of the Republic of India (26 January 1950).
1963: The Naga Hills district becomes the state of Nagaland.
1970: Meghalaya becomes an autonomous state within Assam.
1972: Meghalaya becomes a full state (21 January 1972). Mizoram and Arunachal Pradesh (then NEFA) are separated as {{term:union-territory|Union Territories}}.
1973: The capital moves from Shillong to Dispur.
1987: Mizoram and Arunachal Pradesh become full states.$t$ from public.content where slug = $t$formation-of-assam$t$ on conflict do nothing;
